nfo.\n\nThus: \"I still recommend Candidate B, but we need to explore crew cooperation for A, C, D. I would like to ask Sarah for observations on Candidate A's crew cooperation and adaptability, and Emily for Candidate C's crew cooperation, etc.\"\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B's conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills; A's anticipation of dangerous situations, leadership; C's quick decision making, calm in crisis; D's responsibility, problem solving.\n\nMake a concise argument: B's strengths outweigh concerns, but A's anticipation is valuable but his show-off and closed-mindedness may hinder crew. C's quick decisions and calmness are good but egocentric and unwilling to learn are concerns. D's responsibility and problem solving are good but hot temper and know-it-all attitude are concerns.\n\nThus we still vote B.\n\nNow produce output."}
